Design system
-------------
The grid, type scale and interaction rules are ported from lightphone/light-sdk,
which is MIT licensed. ic_settings_white.xml, ic_back_white.xml,
ic_refresh_white.xml and ic_reply_white.xml (the SDK's ic_directions_uturn_left)
are that project's own files, used unchanged under the same licence, so the bars
look like every other bar on the phone.

ic_archive_white.xml is drawn for this app, to the same 60x60 viewport and 4.0
stroke, because the SDK has 105 icons and none of them is archive. The closest
was ic_trash, and using it would have been a lie: archive moves a message to All
Mail and delete does not.

Sounds
------
All notification sounds are generated at build time by scripts/. No sampled or
recorded audio is included in this repository or in the built APK.

scripts/ref_tracks.json contains measured articulation parameters — formant
frequencies and bandwidths, pitch, level, voicing — derived by analysis from a
reference recording. It is a description of articulation, not audio, and no part
of any recording is reproduced by it or by the synthesizer it drives.
